%I A401388 #22 Nov 01 2026 17:56:31
%S A401388 400,1521,9604,257049,480249,1920996,5659641,43441281,173369889,
%T A401388 693479556,870899121,11095672896,14200058896,16649257024,22187592025,
%U A401388 53251562169,55365148804,355001472400,2796282939681,11185131758724,78362489403081,178962108139584,45101247534114849,180404990136459396,534782061427474809
%N A401388 Squares k, not powers of primes, for which {the largest divisor of sigma(k) that is coprime with k} is a prime power.
%C A401388 If there exists an odd triperfect number (see A005820, A386425) that is not multiple of 3, then it should occur in this sequence.
%C A401388 If there exists a number whose abundancy ratio is 5/3 (see A388016), then it should occur in this sequence (among the odd terms). See Weiner paper.
%C A401388 If there exists any odd perfect number (see A326137, A401067), then its square part r^2 (of the Eulerian form, A228058) should occur in this sequence.
%C A401388 A401375, when applied to these numbers, yields: 961, 61, 2801, 30941, 361, 361, 97, 5229043, 127, 127, 398581, 16129, 917087137, 262209281, 917087137, 3169, 16148168401, 917087137, 5419, 5419, 52379047267, 5419, 262209281, 262209281, 3348577, ...
%H A401388 Masao Kishore, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1090/S0025-5718-1984-0725999-4">Odd Triperfect Numbers</a>, Math. Comput. 42(165) (1984), 231-233.
%H A401388 Oliver Knill, <a href="http://www.math.harvard.edu/~knill/seminars/perfect/handout.pdf">The oldest open problem in mathematics</a>, Handout for NEU Math Circle, December 2, 2007
%H A401388 Pace P. Nielsen, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0602485">Odd Perfect Numbers Have At Least Nine Distinct Prime Factors</a>, arXiv:math/0602485 [math.NT], 2006.
%H A401388 Paul A. Weiner, <a href="https://www.jstor.org/stable/2690980">The abundancy ratio, a measure of perfection</a>, Math. Mag. 73(4) (2000), 307-310. (See Theorem 3, concerning the ratio 5/3)
%F A401388 a(n) = A401386(n)^2.
%F A401388 {k^2 such that A010055(k) = 0 and A401379(k^2) = 1}.
%Y A401388 Intersection of A024619 and A401387.
%Y A401388 Cf. A010055, A401375, A401379, A401380, A401386.
%Y A401388 Cf. A005820, A347383, A347391, A374199, A374463, A379490, A386425 for sequences concerning odd triperfects and A388016 about abundancy ratio 5/3.
%Y A401388 Cf. A326137, A401067 concerning odd perfect numbers.
%K A401388 nonn,more,new
%O A401388 1,1
%A A401388 _Antti Karttunen_, Oct 31 2026
